  "body": "<!--\r\n⚠️ If you do not respect this template, your pull request will be closed.\r\n⚠️ Your pull request title should be short detailed and understandable for all.\r\n⚠️ Also, please add it in the CHANGELOG file under Unreleased section.\r\n⚠️ If your pull request fixes an open issue, please link to the issue.\r\n\r\n✅ I have added the tests to cover my changes.\r\n✅ I have updated the documentation accordingly.\r\n✅ I have read the CONTRIBUTING document.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n### Summary\r\nThis pull request fixes [this terra issue ](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-terra/issues/6850), which was finally not terra-related. With this change, it is possible to retrieve the correct number of qubits when copying a `RawFeatureVector`, and this also fixes actions that involve copying, such as `bind_parameters()`, which currently does not support in-place execution (if I'm not mistaken).\r\n\r\n### Details and comments\r\n\r\nCode to check copying operation:\r\n\r\n```\r\nfrom qiskit_machine_learning.circuit.library import RawFeatureVector\r\nfeature_dim = 4  # dimension of each data point\r\nfeature_map = RawFeatureVector(feature_dimension=feature_dim)\r\nprint(feature_map.draw())\r\nprint(feature_map.num_qubits)\r\ncopy_map = feature_map.copy()\r\nprint(copy_map.draw())\r\nprint(copy_map.num_qubits)\r\n```\r\n\r\nCode to check parameter binding:\r\n\r\n```\r\nfrom qiskit_machine_learning.circuit.library import RawFeatureVector\r\nfeature_dim = 4  # dimension of each data point\r\nfeature_map = RawFeatureVector(feature_dimension=feature_dim)\r\nprint(feature_map.draw())\r\nbound_map = feature_map.bind_parameters([0.25,0.25,0.25,0.25])\r\nprint(bound_map.draw())\r\nprint(bound_map.num_qubits)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis issue was found when looking into these other issues: #180, #95. \r\nCloses #180.\r\n",
